    rdf:value "habits of drinking and smoking, which he indulged in to excess. They arranged terms, $5.00 a week for daily absent treatments. At the end of the week the healer lady heard a great noise in her front hall - a man’s voice threatening her as a cheat and fraud, taking money and doing nothing for it. She came down and found her patient in a rage. She asked him what was the matter, and he said he wanted to drink and smoke as much as  ever.  But, he added, this beastly country is going to ruin - can’t get a decent bottle of whisky in the whole town. “And cigars?” she asked - A volley of oaths against the rottenness of American civilization - not a sound leaf of tobacco to be had for love or money - “I guess it’s all right,” she said “you won’t need any more treatment.” He stopped cursing, gasped, and turned upon her in fury roaring, “ Is this your doing, Madam ?” "^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 74 ;
